#%RAML 1.0
title: ENTSO-E System API
version: v1
description: |
  Thin wrapper over the ENTSO-E Transparency Platform RESTful API.

  Its only job is to speak ENTSO-E's dialect so nothing else has to: it
  holds the security token, translates a bidding zone into an EIC code,
  builds the documentType/domain query string, formats timestamps as
  yyyyMMddHHmm, and converts Publication_MarketDocument XML into the
  canonical model.

  Deliberately absent: caching, aggregation, merging with other sources,
  business rules. Those belong one layer up. If a query parameter is
  needed here that ENTSO-E does not itself understand, the logic is in
  the wrong layer.

  Upstream behaviour this API normalises away:
    - Prices are not timestamped. Each Point carries a position, and the
      instant is periodStart + (position - 1) * resolution.
    - "No matching data found" comes back as an Acknowledgement document
      with HTTP 200 and reason code 999, not as a 404.
    - Timestamps in and out use different formats: requests want
      yyyyMMddHHmm, responses carry yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mmZ with no seconds.

baseUri: http://{host}:{port}/api/sys/entsoe/{version}
baseUriParameters:
  host:
    default: localhost
  port:
    default: "8091"
mediaType: application/json

uses:
  energy: library/energy-types.raml

traits:
  correlated:
    headers:
      X-Correlation-Id?:
        type: string
        description: Echoed into upstream calls and error responses.

/day-ahead-prices:
  description: Day-ahead wholesale prices. Maps ENTSO-E documentType A44.
  get:
    is: [correlated]
    displayName: Get day-ahead prices for a bidding zone and period
    queryParameters:
      biddingZone:
        type: energy.BiddingZone
        default: DE_LU
      periodStart:
        type: datetime
        description: Inclusive. Converted to ENTSO-E's yyyyMMddHHmm UTC form.
      periodEnd:
        type: datetime
        description: Exclusive.
    responses:
      200:
        body: energy.PricePoint[]
      404:
        description: |
          ENTSO-E returned an Acknowledgement document - no published
          data for the requested zone and period. Distinct from a 502:
          the upstream answered, it just had nothing.
        body: energy.ApiError
      502:
        description: Upstream unreachable, or rejected the credentials.
        body: energy.ApiError
      504:
        description: Upstream did not respond within the timeout.
        body: energy.ApiError
